reload: memory indirect operand ([N,sp]) used the stack offset at function entry.

With -fdouble-indirect (on by default) the m68k port allows memory indirect
addresses on 68020+; -m68080 uses them most, -m68060 sometimes. When a pointer gets no register, reload may use the
pointer's stack slot as an indirect address: (mem (reg P)) becomes
(mem (mem (plus sp N))). find_reloads_address computes the slot with the
current elimination offsets (make_memloc) but stores it in the insn only in
the replacing pass (replace_reloads). In the first pass it records no reload,
so calculate_needs_all_insns marks the insn as needing no reloads, no
elimination and no operand change, and reload_as_needed skips it. At the end
of reload the pseudo is then replaced by its stack slot at the INITIAL
offset. Between a call's argument pushes and their pop that is the wrong slot:

    jsr (a0)
    add.l d2,([56,sp])      <- 20 bytes pushed: must be ([76,sp])
    lea (20,sp),sp

Upstream targets without indirect addressing (ind_levels == 0) never take
this path; they push a reload there. ApolloCrossDev issue #27 (reduced from
libjpeg 9 jdsample.c sep_upsample: jpeg_read_scanlines never advanced and
MultiView crashed on JPEGs in ApolloOS R10).

The fix: when find_reloads_address skips the substitution in the first pass
while the offsets are not at their initial values, find_reloads returns
nonzero (operands changed), so reload_as_needed runs find_reloads on the insn
again and the replacing pass stores the slot with the right offset.

Checked 2026-11-17 with cc1 built from gcc-stable plus all Dev patches:
534 C files (libjpeg 9f, libpng, libogg, libvorbis, FreeType 2.14.3,
SDL_image, SDL_ttf, SDL_mixer, SDL_net, timidity, MPEGA, zlib, Lua, the
ApolloCrossDev Projects) at -m68080 -m68881 with -O2/-O3/-Os
-fomit-frame-pointer and -O2: the assembly differs only in 6 operands in
4 compilations, each one corrected by the bytes pushed at that point
(jdsample.c -Os ([60,sp]) -> ([80,sp]), jcprepct.c -O2 ([76,sp]) ->
([96,sp]), timidity resample.c -O2/-O3 ([88,sp]) -> ([92,sp])).
-m68060 -O2 -fomit-frame-pointer: resample.c and jcprepct.c differ, in 5 operands,
corrected the same way (resample.c ([84,sp]) -> ([88,sp]), jcprepct.c
([76,sp]) -> ([96,sp])). -m68080 -fno-double-indirect: no difference.

diff --git a/gcc/reload.c b/gcc/reload.c
index 98cd157c9..8dc41a80a 100644
--- a/gcc/reload.c
+++ b/gcc/reload.c
@@ -148,6 +148,16 @@ int reload_n_operands;
 /* Nonzero means record the places to replace.  */
 static int replace_reloads;
 
+/* Nonzero if find_reloads_address, in a pass that does not replace
+   (replace_reloads == 0), left a pseudo in an address that is valid as an
+   indirect address only through its equivalent memory location, at an
+   insn where the elimination offsets differ from the initial ones.  No
+   reload is recorded for it, so find_reloads must return nonzero: else
+   reload_as_needed skips the insn and the pseudo is later replaced by its
+   stack slot at the initial offset (wrong after pushes, e.g. ([56,sp])
+   instead of ([76,sp]) between a call's argument pushes and their pop).  */
+static int ind_equiv_needs_replace;
+
 /* Each replacement is recorded with a structure like this.  */
 struct replacement
 {
@@ -2666,6 +2676,7 @@ find_reloads (rtx_insn *insn, int replace, int ind_levels, int live_known,
   n_replacements = 0;
   n_earlyclobbers = 0;
   replace_reloads = replace;
+  ind_equiv_needs_replace = 0;
   hard_regs_live_known = live_known;
   static_reload_reg_p = reload_reg_p;
 
@@ -4600,7 +4611,7 @@ find_reloads (rtx_insn *insn, int replace, int ind_levels, int live_known,
 	  }
       }
 
-  return retval;
+  return retval | ind_equiv_needs_replace;
 }
 
 /* Return true if alternative number ALTNUM in constraint-string
@@ -4944,6 +4955,11 @@ find_reloads_address (machine_mode mode, rtx *memrefloc, rtx ad,
 		      /* This doesn't really count as replacing the address
 			 as a whole, since it is still a memory access.  */
 		    }
+		  else if (! replace_reloads
+			   && num_not_at_initial_offset
+			   && ! rtx_equal_p (tem, reg_equiv_mem (regno)))
+		    /* Make the replacing pass visit this insn.  */
+		    ind_equiv_needs_replace = 1;
 		  return 0;
 		}
 	      ad = tem;
